      "id": "vzpb4za",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. WHAT IS SUBJECT–VERB AGREEMENT?"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The fundamental rule of Subject–Verb Agreement requires a singular verb for a singular subject and a plural verb for a plural subject.",
        "Prepositional phrases and misleading polite expressions placed between the subject and verb do not alter the verb requirement.",
        "Indefinite pronouns such as each, every, either, and neither consistently require a singular verb.",
        "Collective nouns take a singular verb when treated as a single unified unit, but a plural verb when referring to individual members.",
        "Units of distance, time, and money representing a single unified concept take a singular verb."
      ],
      "id": "1clu89m"
    },
