      "id": "jmv6xpb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "22. POLITE EXPRESSIONS THAT MISLEAD"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "SSC Frequent Trap: 'A number of' takes a plural noun and plural verb, whereas 'The number of' takes a plural noun but a singular verb.",
        "Watch out for expressions like 'along with', 'as well as', and 'together with'—the verb agrees strictly with the first subject.",
        "Pay attention to the 'More than one' rule: despite its plural meaning, it takes a singular noun followed by a singular verb.",
        "Nouns that look plural but are singular in meaning (e.g., Mathematics, News, Physics) strictly require a singular verb."
      ],
      "id": "e1zrzs9"
    },
